-- title:
--   Existence of good Néron identity component data when J₀(p) vanishes
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Assume two triviality hypotheses: first, for every prime $\ell$ not dividing $p$ and every valuation subring $A'$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ with `A'.LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. with $\ell$ lying in the non-units of $A'$, the group `JZeroC (ResidueField A') p` — the degree-zero part of the divisor class group, namely degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones, of the field obtained over the residue field of $A'$ by adjoining the level-$p$ divisor expansions inside its Laurent series field — has at most one element; second, `JZero p`, the corresponding degree-zero divisor class group of the level-$p$ modular function field based changed to $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, has at most one element. The conclusion is that the type `JZeroNeronIdentityComponentGood p` is inhabited: there exist a scheme $G$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$, a relative group law on it, and a bijection between `JZero p` and the $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-points, satisfying all the requirements of `JZeroNeronIdentityComponent p` (commutativity, smoothness, separatedness, local finite type, quasi-compactness, surjectivity, preconnected fibres, additivity and Galois-equivariance of the point dictionary, Hecke operators realised by endomorphisms, flatness and surjectivity of multiplication by each positive integer, finite index of the subgroup generated by integral sections inside the Galois-invariants), together with, for every prime $\ell\nmid p$, the data `JZeroNeronIdentityComponent.GoodPrimeData` over [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8): a group law and point dictionary on the base change compatible with those over $\mathbf Z$, an `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle`, commutativity, additivity and Galois-equivariance, point dictionaries over each valuation subring above $\ell$ and its residue field compatible with reduction, and Hecke data.
--
--   This is the degenerate case of the construction of the Néron identity component of $J_0(p)$ with good-reduction data at all primes away from $p$: when $X_0(p)$ has genus zero the Jacobian vanishes, and the trivial group scheme over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ supplies all the required data. It is used in the proof of [`ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronIdentityComponentGood`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronIdentityComponentGood), which handles the general level.
